The Python implementation now explicitly filters the only even decimal digits—`2, 4, 6, 8`—which is essential for the `10, 14 -> []` example. I’ve also removed incidental docstring execution from `solution.py`, so the generated AST and the proof term correspond only to executable logic. The proof will characterize the returned list with a mathematical digit-selection function over arbitrary positive `a` and `b`.
